      "cooked": "<p>Broccoli sent me a long list of FAQ-type questions he’d recently received answers for from Chris so I can add some of the answers to my PDF.  One of the answers confused me though:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"10\">\n<li>Several cards have a “search” effect such as “search the trash” or<br>\n“search the deck”, and I assume these effects “fizzle” if the card<br>\ncannot be found in the appropriate pile.  However, other cards have a<br>\n“reveal cards until” effect.  Mostly recently, The Operative reveals<br>\ncards until an Underboss is found.  Do “reveal cards until” effects<br>\ngenerate a shuffle if you reveal the whole deck without finding an<br>\nappropriate card?  If no, then The Operative’s effect is useless once<br>\nall 5 Underbosses are dead, but if yes, then the forced shuffle nerfs<br>\nthe Underbosses’ abilities to find Thugs.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n<p>[quote]Chris:  Revealing cards does not force a shuffle, so you are correct in thinking that The Operative’s Ã¢â‚¬Å“reveal…Ã¢â‚¬Â</p>",
