      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-04-12T22:33:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Well, if you shuffle the trash into the deck, then you’re not revealing cards from the trash, you’re still revealing them from the deck.</p>\n<p>So it sounds like you’re not moved by the argument that revealing a card is essentially the same thing as drawing a card, and if you’re told to draw a card when the deck is empty, then you automatically shuffle the trash to make a new deck so you can complete the draw.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:01:11.463Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 5604,
      "topic_slug": "revealing-cards-vs-searching-for-a-card",
      "display_username": "Spiff",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
